# Cloudflare Pages redirects/proxy rules — mirrors netlify.toml's [[redirects]]
# now that the static site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages while the
# netlify/functions/*.js backend stays on Netlify (see CLAUDE.md, "Hosting
# split" section). First-match-wins, same as Netlify.
#
# REPLACE __NETLIFY_SITE_URL__ below with the real Netlify site URL
# (e.g. https://presora.netlify.app) before this file goes live.

# ── Google OAuth proxy — hides the Supabase project ID ──────────────────────
/auth/callback  https://wxwdymchrmhxeiccnzg.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback  200

# ── Netlify Functions — reverse-proxied so the browser still sees a
#    same-origin /.netlify/functions/* path (no CORS changes needed anywhere
#    in the app's fetch calls). ────────────────────────────────────────────
/.netlify/functions/*  __NETLIFY_SITE_URL__/.netlify/functions/:splat  200

# ── Public API (ApiDocs.tsx) — same proxy target as above, kept as its own
#    clean path per the comment in netlify.toml. Must come before the SPA
#    fallback below. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/api/v1/analyze    __NETLIFY_SITE_URL__/.netlify/functions/api-analyze    200
/api/v1/analyses   __NETLIFY_SITE_URL__/.netlify/functions/api-analyses   200

# ── SPA fallback — every other route is handled by React Router ─────────────
/*  /index.html  200
